! Silicon at the settings of Elk's examples/TDDFT-time-evolution/Si-ramp, for the
! current under a vector potential growing as 0.001 t^2 along x (Elk's ramp, a
! field growing linearly in time).
!
! Matched to the Elk input: the lattice (a = 10.26 bohr), PBE (Elk's xctype 20),
! the unshifted 12x12x12 grid. The cutoff is set by the shift and not by the
! ground state: at t = 500 the field has moved the crystal momentum by
! kappa = 250/137.036 = 1.82 1/bohr, so the frozen sphere's cutoff along the
! field is (sqrt(ecutwfc) - 1.82)^2, 13.4 Ry at ecutwfc = 30.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.26, nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 30.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si 28.086 Si.pbe-rrkj.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 12 12 12 0 0 0
